{
 "format": "cogbench-materials/0",
 "source": "KB materials-reactions.md MVP-40 table (Noita data) + our potions; see .trellis/spec/game-design/v1-scope.md",
 "notes": [
  "index is the u8 cell value used everywhere (grid, recordings, observations); never reorder, only append",
  "fire lifetime is 12-30 frames uniform (DN-MAT-07); whiskey burns through reaction 10, not the burning state",
  "an optional `explosion` object {radius, ray_energy, max_durability, fire_percent} makes a burning cell of that material detonate (FIRE-R10; only gunpowder has one); potions are ours (cf. Healthium, Concentrated Mana, Hastium, Lively Concoction)",
  "flammable_gas has no lifetime (lead decision 2026-10-26): gas pockets placed by world generation persist; gas disappears only by burning or reacting",
  "tag `ingredient` marks the 12 materials the secret recipes are drawn from (water, blood, oil, whiskey, toxic_sludge, sand, coal, gunpowder, gold_dust, bone_dust, fungus_powder, slime); tag `secret_potion` marks the 8 potions that exist only as the product of a recipe (cogbench-rules draws one recipe of 3 distinct ingredients per such potion from the rule seed); recipes are never listed in reactions.json",
  "metal (durability 15) is the alchemy bowl: not corrodible, not burnable, and no blast of the content (bomb 11, explosive projectile + bomb 14) removes it"
 ],
